Root cause:
The bug was caused by a missing call to `dmaengine_unmap_put()`, which is necessary to properly release DMA mappings. This oversight led to a memory leak during RAID6 synchronization, resulting in out-of-memory (OOM) conditions. The patch corrects this by ensuring that the DMA mapping is released, preventing the memory leak.
